From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:20:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: reuse DOOM Eternal's idle client surface across
 VkSurface recreation

DOOM Eternal recreates VkSurfaces along with its HDR swapchains, retaining
references to the old VkSurfaces after their swapchains have been destroyed.
The ref == 1 condition of the old per-window stash served these replacements
from the winewayland driver. Each new client lost the previous wl_surface's
DMA-BUF feedback and replaced its visible subsurface.

That stash is gone: upstream moved Vulkan client-surface creation to win32u
(get_unused_client_surface / use_window_client_surface), and the
presenter-coordination rewrite replaced the old serving function with the
owner model (find_owner / set_owner / activate + active_ref). Port the
carve-out to the new allocation point instead.

Allow DOOM Eternal to reuse an idle cached client despite those old surface
references. The client stays on the in-use list, so the owner model keeps
its ownership and attachment without a detach/reparent cycle; the extra
reference transfers to the new VkSurface as before, and old VkSurfaces keep
their own references. Never reuse a client while busy_ref is nonzero.

Keep the existing reference isolation and detach behavior for other
programs: in particular, Purple's independently reusable graphics probes
must not alias its active game presenter. Do not suppress Vulkan
out-of-date/suboptimal results, disable HDR, or change swapchain image
counts.

This restores the surface-cache behavior needed by this application, based
on the same client-surface caching lifetime support as the existing
patches. It relies on the same Mesa WSI object-lifetime support:
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/34918

Runtime effect on HDR flicker still needs a retest with the game; no game
binaries or installed Proton files are modified.
---

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/window.c b/dlls/win32u/window.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -592,6 +592,31 @@
     pthread_mutex_unlock( &surfaces_lock );
 }

+/* DOOM Eternal recreates its VkSurface together with every HDR swapchain
+ * while retaining references to the old VkSurfaces after their swapchains
+ * have been destroyed. The per-window stash that used to serve such
+ * replacements from the winewayland driver is gone (client surfaces are now
+ * created from win32u), so a replacement VkSurface would always mint a fresh
+ * client surface, losing the previous wl_surface's DMA-BUF feedback and
+ * replacing its visible subsurface.
+ *
+ * Let this one application reuse an idle client surface that is still
+ * referenced by a retained old VkSurface, instead of minting a fresh one.
+ * The extra reference transfers to the new VkSurface as before; the old
+ * VkSurfaces keep their own references. Never reuse a client while busy_ref
+ * is nonzero. Anything else keeps the existing isolation behavior. */
+static BOOL is_doom_eternal_process(void)
+{
+    static const WCHAR doomW[] = {'d','o','o','m','e','t','e','r','n','a','l','x','6','4','v','k','.','e','x','e',0};
+    RTL_USER_PROCESS_PARAMETERS *params = RtlGetCurrentPeb()->ProcessParameters;
+    const WCHAR *p, *name = params ? params->ImagePathName.Buffer : NULL;
+
+    if (!name) return FALSE;
+    if ((p = wcsrchr( name, '/' ))) name = p + 1;
+    if ((p = wcsrchr( name, '\\' ))) name = p + 1;
+    return !wcsicmp( name, doomW );
+}
+
 struct client_surface *get_unused_client_surface( HWND hwnd, int format, BOOL raw )
 {
     struct client_surface *surface;
@@ -608,6 +633,24 @@
     }
     if (&surface->entry == &unused_surfaces) surface = NULL;

+    if (!surface && is_doom_eternal_process())
+    {
+        /* No spare client: share the window's idle client with the new
+         * VkSurface so its wl_surface attachment (DMA-BUF feedback and the
+         * last visible frame) survives the recreation. The client stays on
+         * the in-use list, so the owner model keeps its ownership and
+         * attachment without any detach/reparent cycle. */
+        LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( surface, &client_surfaces, struct client_surface, entry )
+        {
+            if (surface->hwnd != hwnd || surface->format != format || surface->raw != raw) continue;
+            if (ReadAcquire( &surface->busy_ref )) continue; /* live swapchain or drawable, never steal */
+            client_surface_add_ref( surface ); /* new VkSurface takes its own reference */
+            client_surface_update_locked( surface ); /* refresh it before creating GL/VK drawable */
+            break;
+        }
+        if (&surface->entry == &client_surfaces) surface = NULL;
+    }
+
     pthread_mutex_unlock( &surfaces_lock );

     if (surface) TRACE( "Reusing surface %s\n", debugstr_client_surface( surface ) );
